Done. `dispatch` now takes `maxAttempts` (default 3), `baseDelayMs` (default 100), and `sleep` (defaults to `setTimeout`-based promise), validating both numbers up front with `RangeError` before touching the queue. Each job retries up to the limit with `baseDelayMs * 2 ** (attempt - 1)` backoff after failed attempts, records `attempts` on every processed/failed entry, logs exactly once at the final outcome, and keeps `total` as jobs handled. Added seven tests covering retry-then-succeed, exhaustion, exponential delays, `maxAttempts: 1`, per-job attempt counts, and invalid-option queue preservation — all 35 tests pass.
